{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0e75c6122e9494b0ab34b9fd39c54374007406a4e99b7707177fde2ce8f0aa59","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"sa4hnd/vibra-code@0a8524a68899 snapshot 1b89e3adc0f154c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_82557194e87c97183939540bcbfd309fdd5d8363c7894d2ca3a76c5266070349"],"source_ids":["src_98f0d367e9995225afb58cb97dfddc81"],"text":"Vibra Code is an open-source AI app builder: users describe mobile apps in plain English, a backend runs Claude Code inside an E2B cloud sandbox to generate apps, and a live preview appears on the phone.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1d9380c1291c81122dadb9580c9a762d3e92d3f7676a016cd0c487d38887e7d7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"sa4hnd/vibra-code@0a8524a68899 snapshot 1b89e3adc0f154c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a3433ec90b1e16d81263c72c0c11fb4ee79dbffa47aca4469a03c86b3053e98a","slc_ea245923ccf46f44e472522c24db37f20a9e928c26e8e0835db93ba1cb27fa78"],"source_ids":["src_98f0d367e9995225afb58cb97dfddc81"],"text":"The mobile app's core is a native iOS chat UI built with Texture (AsyncDisplayKit) and IGListKit, described as off-main-thread rendering targeting 60fps scrolling.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_445804377daa31d0e9b21d2ebe36cd33324a0cf2295744c91f6c4b09e337bf3d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=skills-patterns","setting":"sa4hnd/vibra-code@0a8524a68899 snapshot 1b89e3adc0f154c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_32393abc0c6d4bfdfd7408f35f0c10768319fb68932d37b7870801dcc2902503","slc_6e52149b213bc21d8de60bd2d7c4c5e2c49d6b05b321915a211267f72a951c0e"],"source_ids":["src_98f0d367e9995225afb58cb97dfddc81"],"text":"Users can describe apps by voice or attach mockup screenshots as input, and generated projects can be pushed directly to GitHub.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5625c342cdfd7f6e6a0b8c3a6f3f1b6eb387742043d92186fde32e3de7859cc9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"sa4hnd/vibra-code@0a8524a68899 snapshot 1b89e3adc0f154c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_188a3d6462cd1cabab888dfb48d782efbf623eca06081d5934e705a63d2db01d"],"source_ids":["src_98f0d367e9995225afb58cb97dfddc81"],"text":"The product supports multiple AI providers — Claude (default), Cursor, and Gemini — switchable with a single environment variable.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6b91b195d318c0d2d0e68d8cac7582c16be658cfa2a30d697f1f39836965398d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"sa4hnd/vibra-code@0a8524a68899 snapshot 1b89e3adc0f154c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0d2213bbd310440f07253bb4638171bb6fa7559f093ab1d5f658f3e1e5a6f6dd"],"source_ids":["src_98f0d367e9995225afb58cb97dfddc81"],"text":"The iOS client exposes modals for selecting the AI provider, browsing generated files, viewing live sandbox logs, publishing to GitHub, haptic settings, and editing environment variables.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_734af18fee98c96bef519d6e82a00427728c9502813ab750ba1362b9f533cdb3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"sa4hnd/vibra-code@0a8524a68899 snapshot 1b89e3adc0f154c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b79cf3e20aa7dfe9fd00042ce71795c775954ea110783ed0e832d5acaedcf423","slc_dc14c92e5ccc4895a89501645f03dc449f4314650be59d4c2a055a38eb05a72a","slc_e9f2bbfd661d0af7851d3efb6cbe9143c0d323ad143bf9f211eb86f604259271"],"source_ids":["src_98f0d367e9995225afb58cb97dfddc81"],"text":"The README positions Vibra Code as an open-source, self-hostable alternative to closed-source AI app builders such as Vibe Code App, Rork, Lovable, and Bolt.new, focused on native mobile apps built with Expo.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_79062d92b4b0075f561ad1c80f8f1dd3a935486c9abb070efaf93bdcbdbae02a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"sa4hnd/vibra-code@0a8524a68899 snapshot 1b89e3adc0f154c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_17775aa237a2217b0aed11f55f1890bb6c617e2ad7340a0cb849380bbbc912ac"],"source_ids":["src_98f0d367e9995225afb58cb97dfddc81"],"text":"Documented flow: the backend creates a Convex session, Inngest spawns an E2B sandbox where the AI agent generates code, updates stream back via Convex, and the phone opens a live preview through a tunnel URL.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c95997c3b33926e0be620488cf9839a1e86e92b65f9571b81c6a16982d43927e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"sa4hnd/vibra-code@0a8524a68899 snapshot 1b89e3adc0f154c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5ddc6812f786eac5c79f0fbf37d607088abc4e037c02273f8e1663419cd1c118"],"source_ids":["src_98f0d367e9995225afb58cb97dfddc81"],"text":"Real-time synchronization is handled by Convex, with changes streaming from the sandbox to the phone instantly.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d0c23800c7a6a68117821473a482035ed58133629e9448735eb5c0bf7e4b53dd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"sa4hnd/vibra-code@0a8524a68899 snapshot 1b89e3adc0f154c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_57e7e6c73d0752300f1e5164758d3301197da0111f0c0a0d2f5f24d8481ab4b1"],"source_ids":["src_98f0d367e9995225afb58cb97dfddc81"],"text":"Chat messages from Convex are rendered as distinct node types: text with markdown, file reads (blue), edits (orange), bash commands (green), todo task cards, and a working-status indicator.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:37:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a8268b2e31604e6781dd950862e3eff5"}
